              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "To log in to your **My Service Canada Account (MSCA)** safely, make sure you use the official Government of Canada website:\n\n\ud83d\udc49 **[Access the official My Service Canada Account (MSCA) Sign-In Page](https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/services/my-service-canada-account.html)**\n\n### **How to Sign In**\nOnce on the official page, you can choose from three secure login methods:\n\n1. **Sign-In Partner:** \n   * Log in using your secure online banking credentials (e.g., RBC, TD, BMO, Scotiabank, CIBC, Desjardins, etc.). No banking information is shared with the government; it simply verifies your identity.\n2. **GCKey:** \n   * Use your Government of Canada username and password. If you don't have one, you can register for a GCKey on the spot.\n3. **Provincial Digital Identity:** \n   * If you are a resident of **Alberta** or **British Columbia**, you can sign in using your provincial digital ID (such as Alberta.ca Account or BC Services Card).\n\n---\n\n### **What You Can Manage in MSCA**\nOnce logged in, you can access and update your information for:\n* **Employment Insurance (EI)** and view your Records of Employment (ROEs)\n* **Canada Pension Plan (CPP)** and **Old Age Security (OAS)**\n* **Canadian Dental Care Plan (CDCP)**\n* **Social Insurance Number (SIN)** details\n* **Canada Disability Benefit**\n\n---\n\n### **\u26a0\ufe0f Security Warning**\nAlways verify that the address bar in your web browser starts with **`https://www.canada.ca/`** before typing in any personal information. Service Canada will never send you unsolicited text messages or emails asking you to click a link to \"unlock\" your account or input your Social Insurance Number (SIN).",
